      "title": "ldaneo: show an expert info if we can't do picoseconds.",
      "message": "ldaneo: show an expert info if we can't do picoseconds.\n\nPut an \"undecoded\" expert info warning into the tree, instead of the\nnanoseconds and picoseconds, if we can't do the 128-bit-divisor\ndivision.\n\nThat also means we *use* the tree, so we don't get \"set but not used\"\nwarnings.\n",
